target:    tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
expect:    P50-the-cut-is-the-min-not-the-last-row-in-the-list
kind:      boundary
rationale: The cut is `min()` under a DESC report and `max()` under ASC — the docstring says so, and adds
           "never `rows[-1]`". Nothing pinned that. Taking the last row in the list instead is the
           mistake a reader makes on the reasonable assumption that a ranked answer arrives sorted:
           it is right whenever the rows happen to be ordered and silently wrong the moment they
           are not, which is exactly the class a differ must not depend on. S4-cut-always-taken-at-
           the-min-01 covers collapsing the cut_side branch; this covers abandoning the aggregate.
---
--- a/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/compare/algebra.py
@@ -571,7 +571,7 @@
     field_name = contract["count_field"]
     counts_a = _ranking_counts(a_rows, field_name, "the first answer")
     counts_b = _ranking_counts(b_rows, field_name, "the second answer")
-    pick = min if contract["cut_side"] == "min" else max
+    pick = (lambda xs: xs[-1])
     cut_a, cut_b = pick(counts_a), pick(counts_b)
 
     if cut_a != cut_b:
